defects.change:
New file engine/editeur/sobriete.py, function relire(reel, template=None, seg=None, tout=False) → French report {retires, deplaces, corriges, gardes, resume, budget, reperes}.

It collects every visible overlay, with the same visibility rules as Reel.tsx:
- broll[] and non-suggested graphics[] (chiffre, coches, carte, motgeant, logo), only when there is no gallery design mode or suppressExtras is false;
- clip emojis, when emoji is enabled;
- styleScenes (notification, metric, paper, product, comparison), except in the editorial mode, where keyword scenes are the subtitles;
- the banner and the 3D intro count as the fixed hook element.

Rules:
- remove an element with no reason: missing source, empty word, empty value, fewer than 2 items, anchor word cut, or a b-roll on a small word or a brand;
- clamp to the duration and stop before the charter outro;
- nothing but the banner during the hook (first sentence, 2.5 to 6 s). A free element up to 1.5 s early is moved after the hook, otherwise removed;
- no b-roll, giant word, emoji or scene on the last CTA sentence;
- the benefits checklist is moved to the solution start. That start is found with « c'est pour ça que », « chez X », « voici », « notre service »… or the first brand after the hook;
- then a greedy pass by priority (logo > chiffre > coches > carte > scene > motgeant > broll > emoji): at most `simultanes` (1) at a time, at least `ecart` (4 s) between two elements, `plans_de_coupe_ecart` (12 s), and at most `par_minute` elements per minute. A free element may shift up to 1.5 s later to fit;
- truncated banner labels on counters (last word a stop word or with an apostrophe) are removed, and 'count' is set;
- with tout=True, a banner ending in « … » is disabled.

Nothing is lost:
- a graphic becomes suggested:true with a 'sobriete' reason;
- a b-roll goes to suggestions.broll;
- a scene gets hidden:true;
- an emoji goes back to suggestions.emojis.

With tout=False, elements without an auto/generated flag (placed by hand, or older reels) are never touched but still count for conflicts. The budget comes from an optional template field 'budget' (defaults: simultanes 1, ecart 4, par_minute 4, plans_de_coupe_ecart 12, accroche_max 6), clamped to safe limits. auto._finish calls relire(r, tpl, tout=True) at the very end (after galerie.prepare/detourage), stores r['sobriete'] and returns the final count of auto b-rolls.

defects.root_cause:
Original bad reel (old code):
- graphismes.suggest old line 63 took the next 3 words as label (« a déjà été », « moins cher qu'un »);
- old lines 70-72 used at=min(found) or 45% of the video, with found anchored anywhere after 3 s, so the list landed during the problem.

Current code:
- graphismes.py:65 label='';
- graphismes.py:71-74 requires all benefits located;
- graphismes.py:76 locates the shock word before 10 s;
- nothing skips values < 2 or the hook.

defects.change:
engine/editeur/auto.py, automatic path. New _banner_ok: the banner is kept only if all of these hold:
- it is one of the LLM-validated headlines stored in suggestions.banners;
- it does not end in « … »;
- it is not the start of the first spoken sentence;
- every strong word (4+ letters, not a stop word) is actually said in the video (exact, or same 5-letter stem).

When the banner is displayed, a new _banner_correct also runs: one LLM call at temperature 0 that first looks for a problem word by word, then returns a corrected title. The banner is kept only if the correction has the same words (accents and punctuation ignored); otherwise there is no banner. Qwen judges badly but corrects well, so a banner it changes is refused.

In every other case: enabled=false and text='' (no banner, never a truncated copy). The check runs after the client charter is applied, which used to re-enable the banner. As a safety net, sobriete.relire(tout=True) also removes a banner ending in « … ».
